del":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"== {{int:filedesc}} ==\n{{Information\n|Description={{en|1=173rd Airborne Brigade}}\n|Source=US Army\n|Author=US Army\n|Date=\n|Permission=\n|other_versions=\n}}\n\n[[Category:USAREUR sleeve patches]]\n== {{int:license-header}} ==\n{{PD-USGov}}\n\n== {{Original upload log}} ==\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|-\n! {{int:filehist-datetime}} !! {{int:filehist-dimensions}} !! {{int:filehist-user}} !! {{int:filehist-comment}}\n|-\n| {{ISOdate|2010-04-23 17:46:55}} || 400 × 343 (43903 bytes) || {{User|Erwin Lindemann}} || ''<nowiki>{{Information&#10;|Description={{en|1=173rd Airborne Brigade}}&#10;|Source=US Army&#10;|Author=US Army&#10;|Date=&#10;|Permission=&#10;|other_versions=&#10;}}&#10;&#10;</nowiki>''\n|}"}}}]},{"pageid":81212279,"ns":6,"title":"File:49th ID SSI.png","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2019-08-10T20:04:49Z","user":"Kges1901","size":83974,"width":758,"height":865,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/49th_ID_SSI.png/500px-49th_ID_SSI.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":421,"thumbheight":480,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/49th_ID_SSI.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/49th_ID_SSI.png/500px-49th_ID_SSI.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":421,"height":480,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/49th_ID_SSI.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/49th_ID_SSI.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:49th_ID_SSI.png","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=81212279","sha1":"d82a1f4053616363d1684bc5a8eb97468307710d","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2019-08-10 20:04:49","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"49th ID SSI","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD US Army USAIOH|Combat service identification badges of United States Army infantry divisions|1949 in heraldry|California Army National Guard Heraldry|49th Infantry Division (United States)","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Description/Blazon\n<p>On a shield 2 1/2 inches (6.35 cm) in width and 2 7/8 inches (7.30 cm) in height divided per bend yellow and red with a 1/8 inch (.32 cm) yellow border, a blue silhouette of a prospector kneeling and panning gold.\n</p><p>Symbolism\nThe shape of the shield has been adopted from the vigilante shield, symbol used by various vigilante organizations during early California history. The prospector is reminiscent of the \"days of 49\" when the discovery of gold in Northern California, present area of the Division, instigated the gold rush, bringing about the necessity for vigilante and other organizations, forerunners of the present California Army National Guard. The colors, red and yellow signify the early Spanish history of the State of California. Blue and gold (yellow) are the traditional colors of the State of California.\n</p><p>Background\n</p>\nThe shoulder sleeve insignia was approved on 5 July 1949. (TIOH Dwg. No. A-1-113)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1949-07-05","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20161205132647/http://www.tioh.hqda.pentagon.mil/Catalog/Heraldry.aspx?HeraldryId=13005&amp;CategoryId=7882&amp;grp=2&amp;menu=Uniformed%20Services\">TIOH</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"TIOH","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/png"}],"revisions":[{"revid":1026447624,"parentid":1026217050,"timestamp":"2025-05-01T05:31:37Z","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"=={{int:filedesc}}==\n{{Information\n|description={{en|1=Description/Blazon\nOn a shield 2 1/2 inches (6.35 cm) in width and 2 7/8 inches (7.30 cm) in height divided per bend yellow and red with a 1/8 inch (.32 cm) yellow border, a blue silhouette of a prospector kneeling and panning gold.\n\nSymbolism\nThe shape of the shield has been adopted from the vigilante shield, symbol used by various vigilante organizations during early California history. The prospector is reminiscent of the \"days of 49\" when the discovery of gold in Northern California, present area of the Division, instigated the gold rush, bringing about the necessity for vigilante and other organizations, forerunners of the present California Army National Guard. The colors, red and yellow signify the early Spanish history of the State of California. Blue and gold (yellow) are the traditional colors of the State of California.\n\nBackground\nThe shoulder sleeve insignia was approved on 5 July 1949. (TIOH Dwg. No. A-1-113)}}\n|date=1949-07-05\n|source=[https://web.archive.org/web/20161205132647/http://www.tioh.hqda.pentagon.mil/Catalog/Heraldry.aspx?HeraldryId=13005&CategoryId=7882&grp=2&menu=Uniformed%20Services TIOH]\n|author=TIOH\n|permission=\n|other versions=\n}}\n\n=={{int:license-header}}==\n\n{{PD-USGov-Military-Army-USAIOH}}\n\n[[Category:Combat service identification badges of United States Army infantry divisions]]\n[[Category:49th Infantry Division (United States)]]\n[[Category:1949 in heraldry]]\n[[Category:California Army National Guard Heraldry]]"}}}]},{"pageid":135828647,"ns":6,"title":"File:85th Civil Affairs Brigade SSI.png","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2023-08-11T17:12:53Z","user":"Coldstreamer20","size":322520,"width":679,"height":904,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/85th_Civil_Affairs_Brigade_SSI.png/500px-85th_Civil_Affairs_Brigade_SSI.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":360,"thumbheight":480,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/85th_Civil_Affairs_Brigade_SSI.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/85th_Civil_Affairs_Brigade_SSI.png/500px-85th_Civil_Affairs_Brigade_SSI.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":360,"height":480,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/85th_Civil_Affairs_Brigade_SSI.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/85th_Civil_Affairs_Brigade_SSI.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:85th_Civil_Affairs_Brigade_SSI.png","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=135828647","sha1":"addc18322f22acbd0a30b5f002291bf154f4151f","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2023-08-11 17:12:53","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"85th Civil Affairs Brigade SSI","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD US Army USAIOH|United States Army brigade Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (SSI)|1976 in heraldry|Civil Affairs Unit Heraldry of the US Army|85th Civil Affairs Brigade","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (SSI) of the 85th Civil Affairs Brigade, part of the United States Army.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1976-08-31","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://tioh.army.mil/Catalog/Heraldry.aspx?HeraldryId=12313&amp;CategoryId=7433&amp;grp=2&amp;menu=Uniformed%20Services&amp;ps=24&amp;p=0\">85th Civil Affairs Brigade Shoulder Sleeve Insignia</a> from the United States Institute of Heraldry website","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:United_States_Army\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:United States Army\"><span title=\"land service branch of the United States Armed Forces\">United States Army</span></a></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/png"}],"revisions":[{"revid":1025165945,"parentid":992185586,"timestamp":"2025-04-27T06:11:58Z","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"=={{int:filedesc}}==\n{{Information\n|description={{en|1=Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (SSI) of the 85th Civil Affairs Brigade, part of the United States Army.}}\n|date=1976-08-31\n|source=[https://tioh.army.mil/Catalog/Heraldry.aspx?HeraldryId=12313&CategoryId=7433&grp=2&menu=Uniformed%20Services&ps=24&p=0 85th Civil Affairs Brigade Shoulder Sleeve Insignia] from the United States Institute of Heraldry website\n|author={{Creator:United States Army}}\n|permission=\n|other versions=\n}}\n\n== Description ==\n'''Blazon'''\n\nOn a purple hexagon 3 inches (7.62 cm) in height and 2 1/4 inches (5.72 cm) in width overall with vertical sides of 1 5/8 inches (4.13 cm), an unsheathed sword on the left and a sheathed sword on the right in saltire with pommels up, both white and garnished by purple, all surmounted vertically throughout by a gold quill with pen to base, all within a 1/8 inch (.32 cm) white border.\n\n'''Symbolism'''\n\nPurple and white are the colors used for Civil Affairs and gold symbolizes achievement.  The swords, symbol of leadership and protection, are sheathed and unsheathed to symbolize the politico-military authority of the organization.  A quill is a symbol of knowledge and alludes to the issuing and dissemination of all directives.  The three charges on the six-sided hexagon with the two swords allude to the unit's present numerical designation.\n\n'''Background'''\n\nThe shoulder sleeve insignia was originally approved for the 362d Civil Affairs Brigade on 31 august 1976.  It was redesignated effective 16 September 2011, for the 85th Civil Affairs Brigade with the description updated.   (TIOH Dwg. No. A-1-595)\n\n=={{int:license-header}}==\n\n{{PD-USGov-Military-Army-USAIOH}}\n\n[[Category:1976 in heraldry]]\n[[Category:Civil Affairs Unit Heraldry of the US Army]]\n[[Category:85th Civil Affairs Brigade]]\n[[Category:United States Army brigade Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (SSI)]]"}}}]},{"pageid":163732185,"ns":6,"title":"File:Hawaii Military Police Brigade SSI.gif","imagerepository":"local","image